
# Shield DJ Lite by Shield-77 — Version History

Formerly known as Shield Player.

## v1.7.4

- Added Long Reverb ON/OFF in Options > Effects, disabled by default.
- Playback time now follows the actual output rate during pitch changes, retaining fractional milliseconds.
- MP3/OGG decoders, Bass Boost, and controls preserved.

## v1.7.3

- Rock EQ now has a more distinct and stable curve.
- Other filters, especially Outdoor, have been rebalanced to remain audible.
- Reverb is slightly more present, with separate decay times for Concert, Cathedral, and Extra.
- Reverb touch bar moved inward, making 0% and 100% easier to select.
- MP3/OGG engine, Bass Boost, and controls preserved.

## v1.7.2

- Reverb maintains its level while decay lasts longer in Concert, Cathedral, Extra, and Custom modes.
- In impulse testing, Extra's reverb tail increased from approximately 0.65 seconds to 1.30 seconds at the −60 dB threshold.
- Peak protection, filters, controls, and MP3/OGG playback preserved.

## v1.7.1

- Added the Classic EQ filter.
- EQ profiles now have more distinct curves; None remains neutral.
- Adjusted reverb to reduce clipped peaks measured during testing.
- All four reverb presets and Custom mode preserved.
- Enlarged the reverb touch area and separated it from the playback seek bar.
- MP3/OGG decoding, Bass Boost, playback controls, and Title ID unchanged.
- DSP processing was measured on PC with test signals. Sound quality and performance still required testing on console at the time of release.

## v1.7.0

- SELECT now opens and closes Options without interrupting playback.
- B returns to the previous page.
- Added audio filters: None, Rock, Pop, Jazz, Clear, and Outdoor.
- Only one EQ filter can be active at a time; Bass Boost remains independent.
- Added Custom Reverb ON/OFF.
- Custom Reverb ON allows free intensity adjustment from 0% to 100%.
- Custom Reverb OFF provides four presets: Off, Concert, Cathedral, and Extra.
- Reverb changes apply when the finger is released from the touch screen.
- Separated reverb and playback seeking touch zones.
- Updated the French/English guide.
- Version number now appears below Shield-77 on the upper screen.
- Bass OFF now disables its filter.
- Removed the decoded-frame counter from the lower screen.
- CIA Title ID preserved for normal installation over Shield DJ Lite.

## v1.6.9

- Restored the playback touch seek bar.
- Touch and drag to preview the playback position, then release to seek.
- The touch controls disabled in v1.6.8 were restored.
- Pitch and L/R track-lock improvements from v1.6.8 preserved.
- Tested on Old 3DS by Shield-77.

## v1.6.8

- More precise pitch display, including values such as 1.05× and 1.075×.
- Pitch adjustment uses steps of 0.025× up to 2.00×.
- Improved L/R track locking with the left Circle Pad.
- Clarified Circle Pad directions in the guide.
- Updated French/English guide.
- Touch controls were disabled in this version and restored in v1.6.9.
- Audio decoding and sound effects preserved.

## v1.6.7

- Added French and English language selection.
- Language preference is saved.
- Added a bilingual startup guide after language selection.
- Holding SELECT during startup allows the guide to be viewed again.
- Guide explains the main controls and features still under development.

## v1.6.6

- Battery information now appears on its own line below the title.
- HH:MM clock preserved.
- No audio or performance changes.

## v1.6.5

- Added an HH:MM clock in the upper-right corner of the top screen.
- Clock refreshes only when the minute changes.

## v1.6.4

- Bug fixes.

## v1.6.3

- Added a +16 dB bass profile between Boost (+9 dB) and Extreme (+22 dB).
- The new profile can be selected using Y during playback.
- The lowest bass level is now displayed as OFF.
- Its DSP gain remained unchanged at +3 dB in this version.

## v1.6.2

- Updated the lower-screen splash artwork.
- Artist credit included in the artwork.
- Original image preserved and adapted to 320 × 240 without distortion.
- CIA internal version: 1110.
- Title ID: 000400000A210100.

## v1.6.1

- Bug fixes.

## v1.6.0

- Major audio stability improvements and bug fixes.
- Added functions intended to prevent audio degradation.

## v1.5.6

- Concert reverb is now more audible, with a smoother echo decay.
- Added short fades between tracks to avoid abrupt transitions.
- Audio buffers are prepared before playback starts.
- Reduced unnecessary DSP adjustments and screen refreshes during playback.
- Enlarged the touch seek bar.
- Dragging the seek bar previews the target time and percentage before seeking.
- Fixed playback counter behavior after seeking.
- Fixed track changes while playback is paused.
- Improved OGG seeking accuracy.
- Seeking in MP3 files without a Xing index may remain approximate.
- Shuffle avoids immediately replaying the same track at the beginning of a new cycle.
- Faster navigation through subfolders without unnecessary SD card rescanning.
- Improved handling of MP3 headers and damaged audio files.
- SD card information and battery temperature remain visible.
- Added a four-page startup guide covering controls and the project.

## v1.5.4

- Reorganized the startup guide into three pages for better readability.
- Holding SELECT during startup allows the guide to be viewed again.
- Slightly softened reverb.
- Added HOME audio boost levels: OFF, 200%, 300%, and 500%.
- Added a limiter to reduce saturation.
- Improved audio resampling during pitch and speed adjustments.

## v1.4.4

- Officially renamed the application edition Shield DJ Lite.
- CIA Title ID remains unchanged to preserve update compatibility.
- Added elapsed time and total track duration in MM:SS/MM:SS format.
- Reduced interface refresh overhead.
- Added the Soft bass preset between Warm and Boost.
- Increased reverb intensity and decay duration.

## v1.3.13

- Added four reverb modes: Off, Concert, Cathedral, and Extra.
- Removed the barely audible Studio and Room profiles.
- Improved file browsing and long filename display.
- Improved handling of Japanese and special-character filenames.
- Improved screen layout.
- Added SD card capacity and free-space information.
- Fixed brightness synchronization so the HOME Menu keeps the level selected in the app.
- Removed the audio meter to preserve Old 3DS resources.

## v1.3.5

- Added reverb.
- Additional bug fixes.

## v1.2.27

- START now exits the application. SELECT is freed up for a future function.

## v1.2.26

- Removed the START shortcut that launched random folder playback.
- Fixed the button prompts displayed on screen.

## v1.2.25

- Red low-battery alert at 20% or less.
- The alert disappears above 20% and when the charger is plugged in.

## v1.2.24

- The library hides folders that do not directly contain any MP3 or OGG files.

## v1.2.23

- Gradual restoration of system brightness when closing the player to prevent a flash.
- The brightness stored by the console remains unchanged.

## v1.2.22

- Increased spacing between commands displayed during playback to improve readability.

## v1.2.21

- Fixed an OGG buffer calculation that could corrupt the end of audio blocks and cause glitches.

## v1.2.20

- Total capacity and free space of the SD card are measured only once at startup.

## v1.2.19

- Display of free and total SD space at the bottom of the upper screen.
- Fixed an issue related to the HOME transition triggered by a brief press on POWER, which could freeze the console.

## v1.2.18

- Pitch and speed range extended from 0.25× to 1.75×.
- Reverted to four audio buffers to reduce reported glitches on OGG.

## v1.2.17

- More robust OGG playback: recovery after certain isolated Vorbis packet errors.
- Increased audio margin to reduce micro-stuttering on Old 3DS.

## v1.2.16

- Added OGG Vorbis file playback.
- OGG files support pitch/speed, bass profiles, and closed-lid playback.

## v1.2.15

- Added EXTREME bass profile (+22 dB), selectable with Y during playback.

## v1.2.14

- Reworked bass equalization with a wider low-shelf filter.
- Increased differentiation between bass profiles.

## v1.2.13

- Display of battery temperature and addition of a thermal alert.
- Alert threshold set to 42°C on Nintendo 2DS Old and 45°C by default on other models.
- Clarified help text: "Plug in headphones before activating sleep mode."

## v1.2.12

- Simplified selection interface: button prompts that cluttered the list are now hidden.

## v1.2.11

- Track list easier to navigate: six entries displayed at a time and increased spacing.
- Track selection highlighted more clearly.

## v1.2.10

- Fixed interface refreshing when exiting the playback screen.
- Long filenames shortened to prevent them from overflowing the screen.

## v1.2.9

- Adjustments to the track list display.

## v1.2.8

- Thermal alert from 45°C on models other than the 2DS Old.
- Temperature updated every 15 seconds.

## v1.2.7

- Display of battery temperature at the bottom left of the lower screen.
- Initial periodic temperature update, every five minutes.

## Features Present Since v1.2.6

- MP3 playback from the SD card, with folder shuffle.
- Continuous playback when the console is closed, with audio output through headphones.
- Pitch adjustment synchronized with playback speed.
- Brightness adjustment directly from the player.
- Bass boost profiles.
- Battery indicator in 5% increments.

The displayed temperature is that of the battery. Thermal thresholds are warnings configured by the application; they do not measure CPU temperature.
